From: VDR-Suite S1 deferred SearchTimer lifetime cleanup
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] epgsearch: reclaim retired CAS rules before global shutdown
Upstream-base: 0118b4129c3601c04c7483f2fd04b604d4a2a980
Apply-after: 0001-0011 in filename order

Native DELETE retains detached cSearchExt allocations so cached OSD readers
cannot use freed memory while the plugin is running. Those objects contain
category allocations released by ~cSearchExt which references global
SearchExtCats. Avoid relying on unspecified cross-translation-unit static
destruction order: reclaim the retired rule list in the plugin destructor,
after native worker threads are joined but while category registries still
exist. The static empty list destructor is then harmless.

diff --git a/epgsearch.c b/epgsearch.c
--- a/epgsearch.c
+++ b/epgsearch.c
@@ -96,4 +96,8 @@
     cSearchTimerThread::Exit();
     cSwitchTimerThread::Exit();
     cConflictCheckThread::Exit();
+    // Retired CAS rules are kept alive for legacy OSD/search readers. Free
+    // them only once the plugin's worker threads have stopped and before
+    // global category registries are destructed at process shutdown.
+    retiredNativeCasSearches.Clear();
     free(ConfigDir);
